<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aulerci</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aulerci were a group of related Gallic peoples in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, named by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. Their branches were the Cenomani around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-mans">Le Mans</a>, the Diablintes around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jublains">Jublains</a> and the Eburovices around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evreux">Évreux</a>, with a fourth, the Brannovices, mentioned once. They joined resistance to Caesar in 56 and 52 BCE, and the names of Le Mans and Évreux derive from two of their peoples.</p></div>
